{
  "actions": [
    {
      "id": "accept_issue_for_intake",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "label `factory` applied by a person on the requester allowlist, matched by numeric user ID"
    },
    {
      "id": "post_comment",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-18"
      ],
      "when": "text passes output_hygiene and secret checks"
    },
    {
      "id": "set_status_or_check",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-13"
      ],
      "when": "result derived from supervisor-observed gate evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "push_factory_branch",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-12",
        "T-24"
      ],
      "when": "branch matches factory/*, diff passes protected_path_check and secret_scan"
    },
    {
      "id": "open_draft_pr",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-18"
      ],
      "when": "branch pushed; body passes output_hygiene"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "freeze_specification",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-01",
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "risk tier at least medium or open questions remain; below that the spec gate decides"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "mark_pr_ready",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires_by_level": {
        "L0": "forbidden",
        "L1": "human",
        "L2": "policy",
        "L3": "policy"
      },
      "threats": [
        "T-14"
      ],
      "when": "policy means the L2 preconditions are satisfied"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "merge_pr",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires_by_level": {
        "L0": "forbidden",
        "L1": "human",
        "L2": "human",
        "L3": "policy"
      },
      "threats": [
        "T-14"
      ],
      "when": "L3 is disabled; a human merge still passes the policy checks and is bound to the head SHA"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "approve_pr",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "reject_or_request_rework",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "pause_or_resume_job",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "cancel_job",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "requester",
        "operator",
        "approver",
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "answer_question",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-01",
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "a person answers the questions of a stage run that waits for a person (the specification stage's clarification, state machine transition S13); the designations are the ones the engine lets answer (Decision::Answer), and the engine also checks that a person who answers as a requester asked for that job; the text is untrusted, at most 900 bytes, becomes a new input of the stage and decides no gate; an answer through the API or the command line never raises a budget ceiling; a pull request or issue comment does not take this verb"
    },
    {
      "id": "write_status_label",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-42",
        "T-43",
        "T-44"
      ],
      "when": "only a label of the factory namespace (prefix `factory: `) that policies/issue-workflow.yaml maps to a job state; never the trigger label, never a `design:` label, never a label of any other kind; written with a token narrowed to issues: write for one repository, and the status comment goes by post_comment; the labels show state and decide nothing; pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0017)"
    },
    {
      "id": "close_or_label_issue",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "none",
      "when": "closing an issue, or a label of the factory namespace that is not a status label (there is none today); the status label has its own row, write_status_label, and the trigger label and the `design:` labels are never written by the factory; pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0017)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "add_new_direct_dependency",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-29"
      ],
      "when": "always, for a package name absent from the base commit lockfile as anything but a member of the project; no allowlist or heuristic approves it; a package first published less than 30 days ago needs a security_approver; the decision is bound to the exact name, version and checksum, and it does not cover the build code of a new package: a build script or a procedural macro that comes in needs its own decision, approve_build_code"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "approve_build_code",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-29",
        "T-30"
      ],
      "when": "always, for each package that is new to the build and has a build script or is a procedural macro, whoever asked for it (new direct dependency or not); the decision is bound to the exact name, version and checksum of that package, and nothing else lifts the block of the semantic check build_script_added"
    },
    {
      "id": "run_fetch_deps",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "none",
      "threats": [
        "T-29"
      ],
      "when": "after dependency policy decision; allowlisted registries only"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "change_protected_path",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human_and_policy",
      "threats": [
        "T-12"
      ],
      "when": "needs spec_authorization AND independent_policy_review AND human_approval"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "grant_tool_outside_manifest",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "use_exec_shell_breakglass",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-06"
      ],
      "when": "per call, single task, recorded"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "widen_egress_allowlist",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "raise_budget_ceiling",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "repo_admin"
      ],
      "id": "install_spec_kit_or_tooling",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "when": "the master prompt forbids running installation scripts without authorization"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "change_authority_allowlist",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23",
        "T-24"
      ],
      "when": "adds, removes or widens a designation; adding or widening security_approver or org_admin needs two distinct org_admins and never self-granted"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "waive_failed_gate",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-13"
      ],
      "when": "only gates NOT listed in security.yaml gate_integrity.nonwaivable_gates; waiver has an owner and an expiry"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "security_approver"
      ],
      "id": "accept_residual_risk",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-31"
      ],
      "when": "owner and expiry recorded"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "send_code_to_new_model_provider",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-20",
        "T-28"
      ]
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "write_to_additional_repository",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-24"
      ],
      "when": "a job is bound to exactly one repository; cross-repository writes are a new job"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "raise_autonomy_level",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-14",
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "moves a repository up the ladder, never to a level that is turned off (L3); a repository capped at L0 is raised from L0; needs step-up authentication; recorded as an audit event"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "repo_admin",
        "org_admin"
      ],
      "id": "lower_autonomy_level",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-14",
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "moves a repository down the ladder; a repo_admin may, and so may an org_admin, which is how the engine decides it"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "unblock_blocked_stage_run",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-13",
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "a person who holds the operator designation lets a BLOCKED stage run go again once the cause is gone: the environment is repaired and the capability re-probe passes, or a decision on the dependency or on the build code it waited for was recorded after the attempt that blocked it (state machine transition S17, guard G_BLOCK_CLEARED_RERUN); the stage runs again and its gates judge the result, so this passes no gate and is not an override"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "acknowledge_documentation_warning",
      "min_level": "L1",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "one decision for each open warning of the reviewer rule `translation-unfaithful` in the gate reports of the evidence the approver saw; approval of the stage is refused while one has none (guard G_APPROVER_AUTHORIZED, ADR 0009 item 17)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "register_repository",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-24"
      ],
      "when": "a person who holds the operator designation registers a repository of the tenant; it starts disabled, at level L0, with no project map; the engine holds no GitHub credential and does not look at the repository, so the installation, the GitHub repository id and the name are what the person says they are. Pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0016)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "confirm_project_map",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "a person who holds the operator designation records the commit of the default branch that holds the project map, after reading the map that was merged by pull request; this is an attestation by a person and not a verification: the engine does not read the repository and does not check that the commit exists or that the map is good. Pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0016)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "enable_repository",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23",
        "T-24"
      ],
      "when": "a person who holds the approver designation lets a registered repository take tickets; refused until a project map commit was attested, and the database refuses the same change for every role. Pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0016)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "operator"
      ],
      "id": "disable_repository",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23"
      ],
      "when": "a person who holds the operator designation stops a repository from taking tickets: its webhooks are dropped and no job can be submitted for it; jobs that already exist are not touched. Pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0016)"
    },
    {
      "approver_roles": [
        "approver"
      ],
      "id": "accept_design_approval",
      "min_level": "L0",
      "requires": "human",
      "threats": [
        "T-23",
        "T-01"
      ],
      "when": "the intake stage lets an issue on the design track start work only when the label `design: approved` is on the issue now, no other design label is, and the person who applied it holds the approver designation, matched by numeric user ID and not narrowed away from this repository; the designation is read from intake_requirements.design_approved_by in policies/issue-workflow.yaml and this row must name the same one. Pending confirmation by the architect (ADR 0016)"
    }
  ],
  "always_human": [
